[{"text":"GA[5, \\[Mu], \\[Nu]] DiracSimplify[%]","anchor":"cb10","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }^5.\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\mu }.\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb10-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GA[6] . GS[p + q] DiracSimplify[%]","anchor":"cb11","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }^6.\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\left(\\overline{p}+\\overline{q}\\right)\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb11-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^7+\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^7\\]","anchor":"cb11-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"The properties of the chirality projectors are taken into account without substituting explicit expressions for \\gamma^6 and \\gamma^7.","anchor":"cb11-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GA[\\[Mu]] . (c1 GA[6] + c2 GA[7]) . (GA[p] + m) . (c3 GA[6] + c4 GA[7]) . GA[\\[Mu]] DiracSimplify[%]","anchor":"cb12","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\mu }.\\left(\\text{c1} \\bar{\\gamma }^6+\\text{c2} \\bar{\\gamma }^7\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }^p+m\\right).\\left(\\text{c3} \\bar{\\gamma }^6+\\text{c4} \\bar{\\gamma }^7\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb12-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[4 \\;\\text{c1} \\;\\text{c3} m \\bar{\\gamma }^7-2 \\;\\text{c1} \\;\\text{c4} \\bar{\\gamma }^p.\\bar{\\gamma }^6-2 \\;\\text{c2} \\;\\text{c3} \\bar{\\gamma }^p.\\bar{\\gamma }^7+4 \\;\\text{c2} \\;\\text{c4} m \\bar{\\gamma }^6\\]","anchor":"cb12-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Moreover, \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\left( 1 \\pm \\gamma^5 \\right)\\) is automatically replaced by \\gamma^{6/7}.","anchor":"cb12-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"(1/2 - GA[5]/2) . (-((a + GS[p + q])/b)) . (1/2 + GA[5]/2) DiracSimplify[%]","anchor":"cb13","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\bar{\\gamma }^5}{2}\\right).\\left(-\\frac{\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\left(\\overline{p}+\\overline{q}\\right)+a}{b}\\right).\\left(\\frac{\\bar{\\gamma }^5}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb13-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-\\frac{\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^6}{b}-\\frac{\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^6}{b}\\]","anchor":"cb13-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Suitable combinations of \\(\\gamma^5\\) will not be rewritten in terms of chirality projectors, if the option ToDiracGamma67 is set to False.","anchor":"cb13-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracSimplify[(1/2 - GA[5]/2) . (-((a + GS[p + q])/b)) . (1/2 + GA[5]/2), ToDiracGamma67 -> False]","anchor":"cb14","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-\\frac{\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}}{2 b}-\\frac{\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^5}{2 b}-\\frac{\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}}{2 b}-\\frac{\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^5}{2 b}\\]","anchor":"cb14-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"However, it the final result must contain only \\gamma^5 but not \\gamma^6 or \\gamma^7, it is better to invoke the option DiracSubstitute67. This way DiracSimplify can perform more intermediate simplifications before presenting the final result.","anchor":"cb14-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracSimplify[(1/2 - GA[5]/2) . (-((a + GS[p + q])/b)) . (1/2 + GA[5]/2), DiracSubstitute67 -> True]","anchor":"cb15","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-\\frac{\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}}{2 b}-\\frac{\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^5}{2 b}-\\frac{\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}}{2 b}-\\frac{\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^5}{2 b}\\]","anchor":"cb15-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"It is also possible to eliminate \\gamma^5 by rewriting it in terms of the chirality projectors","anchor":"cb15-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracSimplify[GA[5, \\[Mu], \\[Nu]], DiracSubstitute5 -> True]","anchor":"cb16","section":"Examples"},{"tex